-- the general form of the diborane argument: a bond incident on three atoms that are pairwise distinct
-- cannot occur in any molecule of the two-centre representation. Delocalized rings and metal clusters are
-- this case, so none of them is a graph object: benzene's six-centre delocalization, the three-centre
-- bridges of the boranes, the multi-centric bonding of (organo)metal compounds that the field says cannot
-- be captured in simple Lewis formulas.
three-centre-not-two-centred : (H : HMol) → (i : hm-bonds H) → (x : hm-atoms H) → (y : hm-atoms H) → (z : hm-atoms H) → isTrue (hm-inc H i x) → isTrue (hm-inc H i y) → isTrue (hm-inc H i z) → (x ≡ y → Empty) → (y ≡ z → Empty) → (x ≡ z → Empty) → TwoCentred H → Empty
three-centre-not-two-centred H i x y z px py pz nxy nyz nxz t =
  case t i x y z px py pz of
    inl q → nxy q
    inr s → (case s of
      inl q → nyz q
      inr q → nxz q)
